# Turn The Course — Project Rules

## Project Overview

Static website for **Turn The Course**, a post-metalcore band from Schweinfurt, Bavaria, Germany.
Hosted via GitHub Pages at [turnthecourse.com](https://turnthecourse.com).

No build step, no bundler, no framework — pure HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript.

---

## Pages

| File               | Purpose                                          |
|--------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `index.html`       | Main landing page (home, music, about, contact)  |
| `tour.html`        | Upcoming and past shows                          |
| `videos.html`      | Video gallery                                    |
| `impressum.html`   | Legal imprint (German law requirement)           |
| `datenschutz.html` | Privacy policy (German GDPR requirement)         |

---

## Tech Stack

- **CSS framework:** W3.CSS (local copy at `css/w3.css` — do not modify)
- **Custom styles:** `css/main.css` — all project-specific styles live here
- **Icons:** Font Awesome 5.15.3 (CDN, `fab` / `fa` prefix classes)
- **Custom fonts:** `Horizon` (regular + outlined italic), loaded via `@font-face` from `fonts/`
- **Body font:** Lato (system/CDN fallback)
- **JavaScript:** Vanilla, single shared file at `js/main.js`, loaded via `<script src="js/main.js"></script>` at the bottom of each HTML file
- **Partials:** Navbar and footer live in `partials/navbar.html` and `partials/footer.html`, fetched and injected at runtime by `js/main.js`

---

## Shared Partials

The navbar and footer are defined once and injected into every page via JavaScript fetch:

- `partials/navbar.html` — the full `<div class="w3-top">…</div>` navbar markup
- `partials/footer.html` — the full `<footer>…</footer>` markup

Each HTML page has two placeholder divs that get populated at load time:

```/dev/null/example.html#L1-2
<div id="navbar-placeholder"></div>
<div id="footer-placeholder"></div>
```

**Rules:**
- All navbar and footer changes must be made in the partials — never in the individual HTML files
- Links in `partials/navbar.html` use `index.html#section` style hrefs so they work correctly from any page
- The `window.onscroll` handler in `js/main.js` is bound only after the navbar partial has been injected, to avoid a race condition

---

## Styling Conventions

### CSS Custom Properties (Design Tokens)
All colours are defined as CSS variables in `:root` inside `css/main.css`:

```css/main.css#L23-31
:root {
  --bg: #0d0d0d;
  --bg-raised: #161616;
  --border: #2a2a2a;
  --text: #e0e0e0;
  --text-muted: #888;
  --accent: #a06cb0;
  --white: #ffffff;
}
```

Always use these tokens — never hardcode colour values.

### Typography
- Headings (`h1`–`h6`): `Horizon` font, uppercase, letter-spacing
- Body text: `Lato`, `var(--text)`
- `h3`: white, `letter-spacing: 3px`, `text-transform: uppercase`
- `h5`: `var(--text-muted)`, `letter-spacing: 2px`, `text-transform: uppercase`

### Layout Patterns
- Page sections use `w3-content w3-container w3-padding-64` for centred, padded containers
- Full-bleed parallax backgrounds use `.bgimg-1`, `.bgimg-2`, `.bgimg-3`
- Full-bleed overlay sections on `index.html` use `.about-bg` or `.latest-bg` (fixed background image + dark gradient overlay via `::before`) — safe to use on interior content divs
- **Sub-page content background:** use `.page-bg` to wrap content sections on sub-pages (`tour.html`, `videos.html`, `impressum.html`, `datenschutz.html`). It provides the same parallax background + dark overlay as `.about-bg` but is explicitly designed for use on a `<div>`, never on `<body>`
- Responsive grid components: `.teaser-grid`, `.member-grid`, `.contact-section` — all collapse to single column on mobile

### Responsive Breakpoints
- `max-width: 600px` — mobile
- `max-width: 768px` — tablet
- W3.CSS responsive utilities: `w3-hide-small`, `w3-hide-medium`, `w3-hide-large`
- Parallax (`background-attachment: fixed`) is disabled on mobile (`max-width: 600px`)

---

## HTML Conventions

- `<!doctype html>` lowercase, on all pages
- `<html lang="en">` on all pages
- All pages share the same `<head>` boilerplate: charset, viewport, `css/w3.css`, `css/main.css`, Font Awesome CDN, and favicon set from `favicon/`
- **Never put any class on `<body>`** — classes that use `position: relative` on `body` create a CSS stacking context that traps `position: fixed` elements (like the navbar) and breaks them. Keep `<body>` plain always
- All `<body>` tags are plain `<body>` with no classes
- For sub-page content backgrounds, wrap the content `<div>` in `<div class="page-bg">` — never apply background classes to `<body>`
- Navbar and footer are **not** duplicated in HTML files — they are injected via `partials/`
- Inline `style=""` attributes are acceptable for one-off layout tweaks (e.g. `style="margin-top: 48px"`)
- HTML is formatted with 2-space indentation, attributes on new lines for long tags

---

## JavaScript Conventions

- Vanilla JS only — no libraries or frameworks
- All shared logic lives in `js/main.js`, loaded via `<script src="js/main.js"></script>` just before `</body>` in every page
- `js/main.js` handles:
  - Fetching and injecting `partials/navbar.html` and `partials/footer.html` on `DOMContentLoaded`
  - Binding `window.onscroll` only after the navbar partial is injected
  - `onClick(element)` — modal image gallery
  - `myFunction()` — navbar style change on scroll
  - `toggleFunction()` — mobile hamburger menu toggle
- Use single quotes for strings (matches Prettier config)
- No semicolons (matches Prettier config)

---

## Prettier Config (`.prettierrc`)

```json/.prettierrc#L1-7
{
  "trailingComma": "none",
  "tabWidth": 2,
  "semi": false,
  "singleQuote": true,
  "prettier.printWidth": 120
}
```

Apply these rules to all HTML, CSS, and JS edits.

