## Running Locally

No build step required. Serve the root directory with Python's built-in server:

```sh
python3 -m http.server 8080
```

Then open http://localhost:8080.

> Note: the partial fetch calls (`partials/navbar.html`, `partials/footer.html`) require a real HTTP server. Opening HTML files directly via `file://` will not work.

---

## Do's and Don'ts

**Do:**
- Use CSS variables for all colours
- Make navbar and footer changes in `partials/navbar.html` and `partials/footer.html` only
- Add new sections following existing patterns (parallax divider → content container)
- Use `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative Font Awesome icons
- Compress/optimise images before adding to `img/`
- Keep legal pages (`impressum.html`, `datenschutz.html`) in German
- Keep all `<body>` tags plain with no classes

**Don't:**
- Edit `css/w3.css` — override W3.CSS rules in `css/main.css` instead
- Put any class on a `<body>` tag — classes using `position: relative` on `body` break the fixed navbar by creating a CSS stacking context that traps `position: fixed` elements
- Use `.about-bg` or any background class directly on `<body>` — use `.page-bg` on a wrapper `<div>` instead for sub-pages
- Duplicate navbar or footer markup in individual HTML files
- Introduce npm, build tools, or JS frameworks
- Hardcode colour hex values outside of `css/main.css`
- Remove or alter the Imprint / Privacy Policy footer links (legally required)